+// llama-kld-swap: load a model once, then evaluate same-type same-size tensor variants by overwriting the
+// tensor data in the loaded backend buffers and re-running the KL divergence against a base logits file
+// (as written by llama-perplexity --kl-divergence-base), without reloading the model.
+//
+// Usage: llama-kld-swap -m model.gguf -c <n_ctx of the base> [usual llama-perplexity options] [--kl-divergence-base base.kld]
+//
+// Commands are read from stdin, one per line, either as words or as a JSON object with a "cmd" key
+// (the "help" command, HELP below, lists them). After the model is loaded, and after every command, exactly one
+// reply line goes to stdout: "@@kldswap {json}" with "ok": true/false and "cmd"; everything else (llama logs,
+// progress, the llama-perplexity style statistics) goes to stderr. Words: "key=value" is a named argument,
+// anything else is positional; paths with spaces need the JSON form, e.g. {"cmd":"patch","name":"x","file":"/a b"}.
+//
+// Tensor placements:
+//   device buffers (CUDA, ...)        written with ggml_backend_tensor_set, read back and compared
+//   writable host buffers (CPU, CUDA_Host; -lm none or -lm dio)    same, plain memcpy
+//   CPU extra buffer types (CPU_REPACK, AMX, ...)  set_tensor repacks the raw GGUF bytes like the loader does;
+//                                     these cannot be read back, so the originals come from the GGUF file
+//   host tensors in a read-only file mapping (-lm mmap, dio+map, lazy tensors)  refused
+//   --moe-cache-mib > 0               refused at startup (the cache keeps device copies of host experts)
+// A name that the model loaded twice (e.g. token_embd.weight duplicated as the tied output) is patched in all copies.
+// Patches live in memory only; the GGUF on disk is never written.
+//
+// Routed gate/up/down experts on plain CUDA devices have individual model-owned weight buffers.
+// Retype and revert verify a replacement before releasing the previous allocation. Other placements use the
+// original slot if it fits, or retain that slot for revert. A placement change invalidates reusable graphs.
+
